window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b277-b83fdf2f5a768504.json"]={sha256:"b83fdf2f5a768504c572edcd1097ab60cff0254aa04060d2682c581c4aaf654f",value:{"id":"b277","title":"河床固床工設計","titleEn":"Riverbed grade-control structures","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"固床工會改變水面、河床及泥砂通量，並非把河床固定後便完成任務。十個單元連結落差配置、臨界水深、水躍、揚壓、顆粒起動、濾層與上下游地形反應，讓學員分辨幾何可行、結構穩定與河道長期平衡三種不同檢核。","summaryEn":"Grade control changes water levels, bed elevations and sediment fluxes. Ten units connect drop spacing, critical depth, hydraulic jumps, uplift, grain motion, filters and channel response. Learners distinguish geometric feasibility, structural resistance and long term channel adjustment, and examine how protecting one location may transfer erosion or sedimentation to another reach.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["落差配置與縱坡","Drop spacing and longitudinal slope"],["臨界水深與控制斷面","Critical depth and control sections"],["護坦揚壓與排水","Apron uplift and drainage"],["濾層粒徑的相容比較","Filter grading compatibility"],["遷移陡坎的追蹤","Tracking migrating bed steps"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["落差配置與縱坡","臨界水深與控制斷面","護坦揚壓與排水","濾層粒徑的相容比較","遷移陡坎的追蹤"],"labelsEn":["Drop spacing and longitudinal slope","Critical depth and control sections","Apron uplift and drainage","Filter grading compatibility","Tracking migrating bed steps"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「落差配置與縱坡」建立原創假想基準，再以「斷面比能的兩種流態」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m；第二組為 y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：固定兩個無因次坡度 S0=0.012 與 Se=0.004，將單一落差 dz 從 0.6 m 增至 0.66 m，L=82.5 m，相較 75 m 增加一成。此為幾何敏感度，沒有驗證較大落差的消能、通行或結構需求。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Drop spacing and longitudinal slope and examine another controlling mechanism through Specific energy and alternate depths. The first inputs and result are dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m; the second are y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Hold dimensionless slopes S0=0.012 and Se=0.004 fixed and raise drop dz from 0.6 m to 0.66 m. Spacing becomes 82.5 m, ten percent above 75 m. This is geometric sensitivity and does not validate energy dissipation, passage or structural requirements at the larger drop.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b277-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「落差配置與縱坡」與「斷面比能的兩種流態」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\" and \"Specific energy and alternate depths\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-01","title":"落差配置與縱坡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「落差配置與縱坡」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固床工把河段總落差分配到構造物與其間河床，先用幾何關係可以檢查配置是否自洽。原坡與目標坡的差值乘以間距，才是單一落差需要承擔的高程差，並非河段全部天然落差。目標坡還受輸砂、河寬與下游控制影響，不能僅為縮短施工量而任意選定。配置圖須同時標出支流匯入、橋梁與魚類通行位置，因為相同總落差的不同分配會產生不同局部影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「落差配置與縱坡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Grade control distributes total reach fall between structures and intervening bed. A geometric balance checks consistency: the difference between existing and target slope, multiplied by spacing, gives the drop assigned to one structure. Target slope also depends on sediment supply, width and downstream control, so it cannot be chosen solely to reduce construction. Map tributaries, bridges and passage routes because different distributions of identical total fall create different local consequences. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「落差配置與縱坡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-01-k1","title":"落差配置與縱坡","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope","text":"固床工把河段總落差分配到構造物與其間河床，先用幾何關係可以檢查配置是否自洽。原坡與目標坡的差值乘以間距，才是單一落差需要承擔的高程差，並非河段全部天然落差。","textEn":"Grade control distributes total reach fall between structures and intervening bed. A geometric balance checks consistency: the difference between existing and target slope, multiplied by spacing, gives the drop assigned to one structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「落差配置與縱坡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\" is correct?","options":["由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距","固床工把河段總落差分配到構造物與其間河床，先用幾何關係可以檢查配置是否自洽。","不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge","Grade control distributes total reach fall between structures and intervening bed.","Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"固床工把河段總落差分配到構造物與其間河床，先用幾何關係可以檢查配置是否自洽。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Grade control distributes total reach fall between structures and intervening bed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b277-v15-02","title":"落差配置與縱坡：定量估算","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「落差配置與縱坡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。適用邊界：均一坡度的幾何初估，不是最適間距或平衡坡保證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m. Applicable boundary: Geometric screening with uniform slopes, not an optimal spacing or guarantee of equilibrium. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。適用邊界：均一坡度的幾何初估，不是最適間距或平衡坡保證。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m. Applicable boundary: Geometric screening with uniform slopes, not an optimal spacing or guarantee of equilibrium.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「落差配置與縱坡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\", which statement holds?","options":["共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。"],"optionsEn":["A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b277-v15-03","title":"落差配置與縱坡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「落差配置與縱坡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。將支流出口與洪水水面另畫，若存在回水控制，應進行水面與泥砂分析後再修正幾何配置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures. Plot tributary outlets and flood levels separately; backwater control requires hydraulic and sediment analysis before adopting geometric spacing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將目標坡改成千分之六重算間距，說明為何落差較少分配給河床時構造密度會改變。畫出末端下切時的可能傳遞路徑，列出必要調查點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Set target slope to six per thousand and recompute spacing. Explain the changed distribution of fall, then sketch how terminal incision could propagate and identify the survey points needed to test that sequence.","failure":"注意干擾：間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。將支流出口與洪水水面另畫，若存在回水控制，應進行水面與泥砂分析後再修正幾何配置。","textEn":"Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures. Plot tributary outlets and flood levels separately; backwater control requires hydraulic and sediment analysis before adopting geometric spacing.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將目標坡改成千分之六重算間距，說明為何落差較少分配給河床時構造密度會改變。畫出末端下切時的可能傳遞路徑，列出必要調查點。","textEn":"Set target slope to six per thousand and recompute spacing. Explain the changed distribution of fall, then sketch how terminal incision could propagate and identify the survey points needed to test that sequence.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「落差配置與縱坡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\"?","options":["以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度"],"optionsEn":["Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b277-v15-04","title":"落差配置與縱坡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「落差配置與縱坡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。診斷應從下游控制與供砂變化回查，而非只補高上游堰頂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream. Investigate downstream control and sediment supply before simply raising upstream crests to restore the profile. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：配置圖須同時標出支流匯入、橋梁與魚類通行位置，因為相同總落差的不同分配會產生不同局部影響。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Map tributaries, bridges and passage routes because different distributions of identical total fall create different local consequences.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。診斷應從下游控制與供砂變化回查，而非只補高上游堰頂。","textEn":"Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream. Investigate downstream control and sediment supply before simply raising upstream crests to restore the profile.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「落差配置與縱坡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。","不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream.","Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b277-v15-05","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「斷面比能的兩種流態」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Specific energy and alternate depths” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"比能以局部河床為基準，把水深與速度水頭合在一起，適合辨認落差上游是否接近控制斷面。矩形河道的單寬流量固定時，同一比能可能對應深慢與淺快兩種水深解；臨界點則是比能最低位置。這裡所稱兩種解不是可任意互換的現場狀態，還要符合上下游邊界和能量損失。河床高程若改變，總水頭必須另加高程，不能直接比較不同斷面的比能數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「斷面比能的兩種流態」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Specific energy combines depth and velocity head relative to the local bed. At fixed unit discharge in a rectangular channel, one energy level can correspond to a deep slow or shallow fast depth, while the minimum defines critical flow. These alternate depths are not freely interchangeable field states; boundary conditions and losses select the actual solution. When bed elevation changes, include elevation in total head rather than comparing specific energy values from different sections directly. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Specific energy and alternate depths” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「斷面比能的兩種流態」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Specific energy and alternate depths”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-05-k1","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths","text":"比能以局部河床為基準，把水深與速度水頭合在一起，適合辨認落差上游是否接近控制斷面。矩形河道的單寬流量固定時，同一比能可能對應深慢與淺快兩種水深解；臨界點則是比能最低位置。","textEn":"Specific energy combines depth and velocity head relative to the local bed. At fixed unit discharge in a rectangular channel, one energy level can correspond to a deep slow or shallow fast depth, while the minimum defines critical flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「斷面比能的兩種流態」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Specific energy and alternate depths\" is correct?","options":["不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","比能以局部河床為基準，把水深與速度水頭合在一起，適合辨認落差上游是否接近控制斷面。"],"optionsEn":["Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","Specific energy combines depth and velocity head relative to the local bed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比能以局部河床為基準，把水深與速度水頭合在一起，適合辨認落差上游是否接近控制斷面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Specific energy combines depth and velocity head relative to the local bed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b277-v15-06","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態：定量估算","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷面比能的兩種流態」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Specific energy and alternate depths” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。適用邊界：矩形斷面、速度分布係數取一且近似靜水壓，未包含局部損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m. Applicable boundary: Rectangular section with unit velocity correction and approximately hydrostatic pressure, excluding local losses. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。適用邊界：矩形斷面、速度分布係數取一且近似靜水壓，未包含局部損失。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m. Applicable boundary: Rectangular section with unit velocity correction and approximately hydrostatic pressure, excluding local losses.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「斷面比能的兩種流態」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Specific energy and alternate depths\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓","任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m.","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition","Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b277-v15-07","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷面比能的兩種流態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Specific energy and alternate depths” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。不同測站需加回各自床高才能比較總水頭，若發現表面落差卻無對應能損，先核對基準與量測位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve. Add bed elevation at each station before comparing total head. Apparent inconsistencies require checks of datum and measurement location before interpreting losses. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持單寬流量不變，另算一個較深水深的比能並畫在曲線上。把兩斷面床高也列入帳表，說明哪些組合需要能量輸入才可能成立。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep unit discharge fixed and calculate specific energy at a greater depth. Plot both points and add bed elevations in a head ledger, explaining which combinations would require an external energy input.","failure":"注意干擾：在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。不同測站需加回各自床高才能比較總水頭，若發現表面落差卻無對應能損，先核對基準與量測位置。","textEn":"Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve. Add bed elevation at each station before comparing total head. Apparent inconsistencies require checks of datum and measurement location before interpreting losses.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持單寬流量不變，另算一個較深水深的比能並畫在曲線上。把兩斷面床高也列入帳表，說明哪些組合需要能量輸入才可能成立。","textEn":"Keep unit discharge fixed and calculate specific energy at a greater depth. Plot both points and add bed elevations in a head ledger, explaining which combinations would require an external energy input.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「斷面比能的兩種流態」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Specific energy and alternate depths\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve.","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape"],"answer":1,"explanation":"量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b277-v15-08","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態：失效診斷","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷面比能的兩種流態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Specific energy and alternate depths” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。應移到壓力分布較合理的斷面，或改用能描述非靜水效應的模型。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth. Move the section to a suitable location or use a model resolving nonhydrostatic pressure and vertical acceleration. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：河床高程若改變，總水頭必須另加高程，不能直接比較不同斷面的比能數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: When bed elevation changes, include elevation in total head rather than comparing specific energy values from different sections directly.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。應移到壓力分布較合理的斷面，或改用能描述非靜水效應的模型。","textEn":"Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth. Move the section to a suitable location or use a model resolving nonhydrostatic pressure and vertical acceleration.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「斷面比能的兩種流態」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Specific energy and alternate depths\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b277-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「臨界水深與控制斷面」與「水躍共軛水深」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Critical depth and control sections\" and \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-09","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「臨界水深與控制斷面」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Critical depth and control sections” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在矩形斷面中，比能對水深的斜率為零可導出臨界水深，對應水流傳播速度與重力波速的關係。它提供流態分界，但不代表構造物每個位置都會自動達到臨界。寬頂、收縮與下游淹沒情況會決定控制是否存在；若下游水位足夠高，原先假設的自由控制可能被淹沒。解題應先畫水面與床面，再判斷控制位置，最後才帶入單寬流量計算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「臨界水深與控制斷面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Critical depth follows from the minimum of specific energy in a rectangular section and relates flow speed to gravity-wave propagation. It marks a regime boundary, not a state that every point near a structure automatically reaches. Crest length, contraction and downstream submergence determine whether a control exists. High tailwater can drown a presumed free control. Draw bed and water surfaces, identify a defensible control location, and only then apply unit discharge. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Critical depth and control sections” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「臨界水深與控制斷面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Critical depth and control sections”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-09-k1","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections","text":"在矩形斷面中，比能對水深的斜率為零可導出臨界水深，對應水流傳播速度與重力波速的關係。它提供流態分界，但不代表構造物每個位置都會自動達到臨界。","textEn":"Critical depth follows from the minimum of specific energy in a rectangular section and relates flow speed to gravity-wave propagation. It marks a regime boundary, not a state that every point near a structure automatically reaches.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「臨界水深與控制斷面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Critical depth and control sections\" is correct?","options":["在矩形斷面中，比能對水深的斜率為零可導出臨界水深，對應水流傳播速度與重力波速的關係。","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠"],"optionsEn":["Critical depth follows from the minimum of specific energy in a rectangular section and relates flow speed to gravity-wave propagation.","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在矩形斷面中，比能對水深的斜率為零可導出臨界水深，對應水流傳播速度與重力波速的關係。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Critical depth follows from the minimum of specific energy in a rectangular section and relates flow speed to gravity-wave propagation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b277-v15-10","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面：定量估算","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「臨界水深與控制斷面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Critical depth and control sections” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。適用邊界：矩形斷面之臨界水深，不能直接套用梯形斷面或淹沒控制。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m. Applicable boundary: Critical depth for a rectangular section, not directly transferable to trapezoidal sections or drowned controls. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。適用邊界：矩形斷面之臨界水深，不能直接套用梯形斷面或淹沒控制。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m. Applicable boundary: Critical depth for a rectangular section, not directly transferable to trapezoidal sections or drowned controls.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「臨界水深與控制斷面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Critical depth and control sections\", which statement holds?","options":["同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度"],"optionsEn":["One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b277-v15-11","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「臨界水深與控制斷面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Critical depth and control sections” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。同步量測上下游水位與流量，若尾水改變已影響控制區，就應標記淹沒轉換，不再使用單一自由出流假設外推全部工況。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable. Record both water levels and discharge. Once tailwater influences the control region, identify the submergence transition instead of extrapolating a free-flow assumption. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將單寬流量增加一倍重算臨界水深，與水深也增加一倍的直覺比較。補畫自由與淹沒兩種尾水情境，指出公式仍有效與失去控制意義的位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double unit discharge and compare the calculated critical depth with a doubled-depth guess. Sketch free and submerged tailwater conditions and identify where the formula remains valid but no longer defines an actual control.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。同步量測上下游水位與流量，若尾水改變已影響控制區，就應標記淹沒轉換，不再使用單一自由出流假設外推全部工況。","textEn":"Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable. Record both water levels and discharge. Once tailwater influences the control region, identify the submergence transition instead of extrapolating a free-flow assumption.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將單寬流量增加一倍重算臨界水深，與水深也增加一倍的直覺比較。補畫自由與淹沒兩種尾水情境，指出公式仍有效與失去控制意義的位置。","textEn":"Double unit discharge and compare the calculated critical depth with a doubled-depth guess. Sketch free and submerged tailwater conditions and identify where the formula remains valid but no longer defines an actual control.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「臨界水深與控制斷面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Critical depth and control sections\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度","在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration","Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b277-v15-12","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「臨界水深與控制斷面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Critical depth and control sections” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。若洪峰時水面連續跨越構造，應檢查淹沒而非只懷疑流量儀器失準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater. A continuous flood water surface across the structure warrants checking drowning before assuming that discharge instrumentation has failed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解題應先畫水面與床面，再判斷控制位置，最後才帶入單寬流量計算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Draw bed and water surfaces, identify a defensible control location, and only then apply unit discharge.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。若洪峰時水面連續跨越構造，應檢查淹沒而非只懷疑流量儀器失準。","textEn":"Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater. A continuous flood water surface across the structure warrants checking drowning before assuming that discharge instrumentation has failed.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「臨界水深與控制斷面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Critical depth and control sections\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough"],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b277-v15-13","title":"水躍共軛水深：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「水躍共軛水深」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固床下游的急流可能透過水躍轉成緩流，過程中動量關係可求前後共軛水深，但機械能會耗散。公式假設短距離、矩形斷面與近似水平底床，不能把結果當成消能池長度或護坦厚度。尾水太低時水躍可能向下游移出保護區，太高則呈不同淹沒狀態。設計檢查須同時追蹤流量與尾水組合，並留意脈動壓力對接縫與塊石的反覆作用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水躍共軛水深」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A hydraulic jump can convert supercritical flow below grade control into subcritical flow. Momentum gives conjugate depths while mechanical energy dissipates. The standard relation assumes a short, horizontal, rectangular reach and does not determine basin length or apron thickness. Low tailwater may sweep the jump beyond protection; higher tailwater changes submergence. Examine combinations of discharge and tailwater, including fluctuating pressures acting repeatedly on joints and loose stones, rather than checking one nominal operating point. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水躍共軛水深」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-13-k1","title":"水躍共軛水深","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump","text":"固床下游的急流可能透過水躍轉成緩流，過程中動量關係可求前後共軛水深，但機械能會耗散。公式假設短距離、矩形斷面與近似水平底床，不能把結果當成消能池長度或護坦厚度。","textEn":"A hydraulic jump can convert supercritical flow below grade control into subcritical flow. Momentum gives conjugate depths while mechanical energy dissipates.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水躍共軛水深」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\" is correct?","options":["共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠","固床下游的急流可能透過水躍轉成緩流，過程中動量關係可求前後共軛水深，但機械能會耗散。","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓"],"optionsEn":["A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough","A hydraulic jump can convert supercritical flow below grade control into subcritical flow.","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"固床下游的急流可能透過水躍轉成緩流，過程中動量關係可求前後共軛水深，但機械能會耗散。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A hydraulic jump can convert supercritical flow below grade control into subcritical flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b277-v15-14","title":"水躍共軛水深：定量估算","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水躍共軛水深」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。適用邊界：水平矩形短水躍，未給消能池長度且忽略外加阻力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m. Applicable boundary: Short hydraulic jump in a horizontal rectangular reach, without basin length or external resisting forces. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。適用邊界：水平矩形短水躍，未給消能池長度且忽略外加阻力。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m. Applicable boundary: Short hydraulic jump in a horizontal rectangular reach, without basin length or external resisting forces.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水躍共軛水深」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\", which statement holds?","options":["任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。"],"optionsEn":["Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b277-v15-15","title":"水躍共軛水深：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水躍共軛水深」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。以動量計算和實測後水深比較，若偏差大先查坡度、側壁與阻力影響，再決定是否需實體水工模型。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range. Compare momentum prediction with downstream depth. Large differences require checking bed slope, sidewalls and resistance before considering a physical hydraulic model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持急流水深不變將速度降低一成重算，並比較兩種尾水高度。畫出水躍可能離開護坦的情況，列出除了水深外還應觀測的三項量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce approach velocity by ten percent at fixed depth and recalculate. Compare two tailwater levels, sketch a jump leaving the apron, and list three observations needed in addition to water depth.","failure":"注意干擾：若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。以動量計算和實測後水深比較，若偏差大先查坡度、側壁與阻力影響，再決定是否需實體水工模型。","textEn":"Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range. Compare momentum prediction with downstream depth. Large differences require checking bed slope, sidewalls and resistance before considering a physical hydraulic model.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持急流水深不變將速度降低一成重算，並比較兩種尾水高度。畫出水躍可能離開護坦的情況，列出除了水深外還應觀測的三項量。","textEn":"Reduce approach velocity by ten percent at fixed depth and recalculate. Compare two tailwater levels, sketch a jump leaving the apron, and list three observations needed in addition to water depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水躍共軛水深」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\"?","options":["同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距"],"optionsEn":["Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b277-v15-16","title":"水躍共軛水深：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水躍共軛水深」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。下游集中沖坑與水躍前緣移動是比平均水深更直接的警訊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron. A concentrated scour hole and migrating jump front provide more direct warning than mean depth. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計檢查須同時追蹤流量與尾水組合，並留意脈動壓力對接縫與塊石的反覆作用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Examine combinations of discharge and tailwater, including fluctuating pressures acting repeatedly on joints and loose stones, rather than checking one nominal operating point.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。下游集中沖坑與水躍前緣移動是比平均水深更直接的警訊。","textEn":"Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron. A concentrated scour hole and migrating jump front provide more direct warning than mean depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水躍共軛水深」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron.","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b277-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「護坦揚壓與排水」與「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Apron uplift and drainage\" and \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-17","title":"護坦揚壓與排水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「護坦揚壓與排水」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Apron uplift and drainage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水可能從構造上游滲到護坦下方，形成向上的孔隙水壓；下游水深增加時，上表面也會受到水壓，必須用淨值比較。沿底板線性下降的壓力分布只是可檢核的簡化假設，接縫漏水、排水失效與地層不均會改變形狀。總揚力由壓力積分取得，接著還要檢查偏心力矩與局部裂縫。單純增加重量可能轉移地基問題，因此排水與截水的效果應以孔壓量測驗證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「護坦揚壓與排水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Seepage can press upward beneath an apron, while tailwater also loads its upper surface; resistance must be compared with net pressure. A linear underside pressure distribution is a checkable simplification that joints, blocked drains and heterogeneous strata may invalidate. Integrating pressure gives total uplift, after which moments and local cracking still need evaluation. Adding weight can transfer problems to the foundation, so verify drainage and cutoffs through measured pore pressures rather than assumed effectiveness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Apron uplift and drainage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「護坦揚壓與排水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Apron uplift and drainage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-17-k1","title":"護坦揚壓與排水","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage","text":"水可能從構造上游滲到護坦下方，形成向上的孔隙水壓；下游水深增加時，上表面也會受到水壓，必須用淨值比較。沿底板線性下降的壓力分布只是可檢核的簡化假設，接縫漏水、排水失效與地層不均會改變形狀。","textEn":"Seepage can press upward beneath an apron, while tailwater also loads its upper surface; resistance must be compared with net pressure. A linear underside pressure distribution is a checkable simplification that joints, blocked drains and heterogeneous strata may invalidate.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「護坦揚壓與排水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Apron uplift and drainage\" is correct?","options":["護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","水可能從構造上游滲到護坦下方，形成向上的孔隙水壓；下游水深增加時，上表面也會受到水壓，必須用淨值比較。"],"optionsEn":["Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Seepage can press upward beneath an apron, while tailwater also loads its upper surface; resistance must be compared with net pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水可能從構造上游滲到護坦下方，形成向上的孔隙水壓；下游水深增加時，上表面也會受到水壓，必須用淨值比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Seepage can press upward beneath an apron, while tailwater also loads its upper surface; resistance must be compared with net pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b277-v15-18","title":"護坦揚壓與排水：定量估算","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「護坦揚壓與排水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Apron uplift and drainage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。適用邊界：給定的是板底淨向上壓力且沿長度線性變化，未檢查板彎曲。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN. Applicable boundary: Specified values are net upward pressures varying linearly along length; slab bending is not checked. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。適用邊界：給定的是板底淨向上壓力且沿長度線性變化，未檢查板彎曲。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN. Applicable boundary: Specified values are net upward pressures varying linearly along length; slab bending is not checked.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「護坦揚壓與排水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Apron uplift and drainage\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度","兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location","The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b277-v15-19","title":"護坦揚壓與排水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「護坦揚壓與排水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Apron uplift and drainage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。檢查排水出口通暢及流量變化，若中部壓力高於線性假設，應修正積分分布並檢查接縫漏水。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it. Confirm net pressure and inspect drain flow. A middle pressure exceeding the assumed line requires revising the integrated distribution and checking joints. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設下游淨壓力增加一倍而上游不變，重算揚力並比較作用位置。提出至少兩個能區分排水堵塞與河水位上升的量測組合。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double downstream net pressure while keeping upstream pressure fixed. Recalculate uplift and compare its location, then propose at least two measurement combinations that distinguish blocked drainage from a rise in river stage.","failure":"注意干擾：排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。檢查排水出口通暢及流量變化，若中部壓力高於線性假設，應修正積分分布並檢查接縫漏水。","textEn":"Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it. Confirm net pressure and inspect drain flow. A middle pressure exceeding the assumed line requires revising the integrated distribution and checking joints.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設下游淨壓力增加一倍而上游不變，重算揚力並比較作用位置。提出至少兩個能區分排水堵塞與河水位上升的量測組合。","textEn":"Double downstream net pressure while keeping upstream pressure fixed. Recalculate uplift and compare its location, then propose at least two measurement combinations that distinguish blocked drainage from a rise in river stage.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「護坦揚壓與排水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Apron uplift and drainage\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。","不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it.","Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b277-v15-20","title":"護坦揚壓與排水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「護坦揚壓與排水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Apron uplift and drainage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。應把孔壓上升與裂縫變化連續比對，防止誤當正常水位波動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage. Opening joints can then admit more water, so compare pressure increases with crack changes rather than dismissing them as ordinary stage fluctuations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單純增加重量可能轉移地基問題，因此排水與截水的效果應以孔壓量測驗證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Adding weight can transfer problems to the foundation, so verify drainage and cutoffs through measured pore pressures rather than assumed effectiveness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。應把孔壓上升與裂縫變化連續比對，防止誤當正常水位波動。","textEn":"Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage. Opening joints can then admit more water, so compare pressure increases with crack changes rather than dismissing them as ordinary stage fluctuations.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「護坦揚壓與排水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Apron uplift and drainage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b277-v15-21","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grain motion and Shields parameter” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"非黏性床料的起動可用水流剪力相對於顆粒浸水重量尺度來表示，形成無因次希爾茲參數。粒徑代表方式、顆粒排列、隱蔽效應與流況會影響臨界判斷，不能把任何單一數字稱為所有材料的法定安全界線。起動也不等同整個河段的輸砂量，少量細粒先動可能改變裝甲層。解題應先說明床料是否非黏性，再選與輸砂關係相容的臨界描述。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For noncohesive sediment, Shields stress compares fluid shear with a submerged grain-weight scale. Grain-size representation, packing, hiding and flow conditions affect the threshold, so no single number is a universal statutory limit for every bed material. Incipient movement also differs from reach sediment transport; early removal of fines may alter armouring. Identify whether the bed is noncohesive and choose a threshold description consistent with the transport relation before interpreting the dimensionless result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grain motion and Shields parameter” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grain motion and Shields parameter”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-21-k1","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter","text":"非黏性床料的起動可用水流剪力相對於顆粒浸水重量尺度來表示，形成無因次希爾茲參數。粒徑代表方式、顆粒排列、隱蔽效應與流況會影響臨界判斷，不能把任何單一數字稱為所有材料的法定安全界線。","textEn":"For noncohesive sediment, Shields stress compares fluid shear with a submerged grain-weight scale. Grain-size representation, packing, hiding and flow conditions affect the threshold, so no single number is a universal statutory limit for every bed material.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\" is correct?","options":["非黏性床料的起動可用水流剪力相對於顆粒浸水重量尺度來表示，形成無因次希爾茲參數。","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全"],"optionsEn":["For noncohesive sediment, Shields stress compares fluid shear with a submerged grain-weight scale.","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety"],"answer":0,"explanation":"非黏性床料的起動可用水流剪力相對於顆粒浸水重量尺度來表示，形成無因次希爾茲參數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For noncohesive sediment, Shields stress compares fluid shear with a submerged grain-weight scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b277-v15-22","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數：定量估算","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grain motion and Shields parameter” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。適用邊界：只計非黏性顆粒之無因次應力，沒有指定通用起動門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Calculates dimensionless stress for noncohesive grains without specifying a universal entrainment threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。適用邊界：只計非黏性顆粒之無因次應力，沒有指定通用起動門檻。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Calculates dimensionless stress for noncohesive grains without specifying a universal entrainment threshold.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\", which statement holds?","options":["只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距"],"optionsEn":["Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b277-v15-23","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grain motion and Shields parameter” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。用標記顆粒或短時攝影追蹤起動，並記錄先動粒徑；若床料含黏土或根系，須另評估其凝聚與補強效應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth. Track first movement with marked grains or short video sequences and record moving sizes. Clay or roots require separate cohesion or reinforcement assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將粒徑減半而剪力不變重算參數，說明數值變化為何仍不足以求出輸砂量。列出建立輸砂關係前需要補齊的床料與流況資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve grain diameter at fixed stress and recalculate. Explain why the changed parameter still does not supply transport rate, and list the sediment and flow information needed before selecting a transport relationship.","failure":"注意干擾：把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。用標記顆粒或短時攝影追蹤起動，並記錄先動粒徑；若床料含黏土或根系，須另評估其凝聚與補強效應。","textEn":"Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth. Track first movement with marked grains or short video sequences and record moving sizes. Clay or roots require separate cohesion or reinforcement assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將粒徑減半而剪力不變重算參數，說明數值變化為何仍不足以求出輸砂量。列出建立輸砂關係前需要補齊的床料與流況資料。","textEn":"Halve grain diameter at fixed stress and recalculate. Explain why the changed parameter still does not supply transport rate, and list the sediment and flow information needed before selecting a transport relationship.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b277-v15-24","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grain motion and Shields parameter” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。若表面粗化卻下方出現空洞，應查分選與內部流失而非只看粗粒未移動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains. Surface coarsening with subsurface voids calls for checking sorting and internal loss, even if large particles remain stationary. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解題應先說明床料是否非黏性，再選與輸砂關係相容的臨界描述。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Identify whether the bed is noncohesive and choose a threshold description consistent with the transport relation before interpreting the dimensionless result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。若表面粗化卻下方出現空洞，應查分選與內部流失而非只看粗粒未移動。","textEn":"A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains. Surface coarsening with subsurface voids calls for checking sorting and internal loss, even if large particles remain stationary.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全"],"optionsEn":["A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b277-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「濾層粒徑的相容比較」與「河床泥砂收支」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Filter grading compatibility\" and \"Bed sediment continuity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-25","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「濾層粒徑的相容比較」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Filter grading compatibility” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"護坦或塊石下的濾層需要讓水通過，同時限制細土被帶出，保土與透水是兩個相互牽制的功能。粒徑分位數比值可以協助比較級配，但選用哪一種準則仍取決於土質、流向、分散性與設施規範。單一比值不能驗證厚度、離析或施工破損。檢查應連結基土和濾料的完整級配曲線，再用代表水力梯度的試驗觀察濁度、流量與壓力是否穩定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「濾層粒徑的相容比較」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A filter beneath stone or concrete must pass water while retaining base soil, creating competing permeability and retention requirements. Ratios of grading percentiles help compare materials, but the applicable criteria depend on soil behaviour, flow direction, dispersivity and project requirements. One ratio does not verify thickness, segregation or construction damage. Compare complete grading curves and use tests at representative hydraulic gradients to observe whether turbidity, discharge and pressure stabilize rather than relying only on sieve labels. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filter grading compatibility” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「濾層粒徑的相容比較」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filter grading compatibility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-25-k1","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility","text":"護坦或塊石下的濾層需要讓水通過，同時限制細土被帶出，保土與透水是兩個相互牽制的功能。粒徑分位數比值可以協助比較級配，但選用哪一種準則仍取決於土質、流向、分散性與設施規範。","textEn":"A filter beneath stone or concrete must pass water while retaining base soil, creating competing permeability and retention requirements. Ratios of grading percentiles help compare materials, but the applicable criteria depend on soil behaviour, flow direction, dispersivity and project requirements.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「濾層粒徑的相容比較」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Filter grading compatibility\" is correct?","options":["任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全","護坦或塊石下的濾層需要讓水通過，同時限制細土被帶出，保土與透水是兩個相互牽制的功能。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度"],"optionsEn":["Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety","A filter beneath stone or concrete must pass water while retaining base soil, creating competing permeability and retention requirements.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"護坦或塊石下的濾層需要讓水通過，同時限制細土被帶出，保土與透水是兩個相互牽制的功能。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A filter beneath stone or concrete must pass water while retaining base soil, creating competing permeability and retention requirements. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b277-v15-26","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較：定量估算","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濾層粒徑的相容比較」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Filter grading compatibility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。適用邊界：純級配比值示例，不宣稱四就是任意基土之合格門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: A grading ratio example only; four is not asserted as an acceptance threshold for arbitrary soils. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。適用邊界：純級配比值示例，不宣稱四就是任意基土之合格門檻。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: A grading ratio example only; four is not asserted as an acceptance threshold for arbitrary soils.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「濾層粒徑的相容比較」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Filter grading compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度","不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration","Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b277-v15-27","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「濾層粒徑的相容比較」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filter grading compatibility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。另量施工厚度並檢查離析，必要時在試驗柱施加逐級水頭，觀察出水含砂及壓差，將材料相容與施工品質分開驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units. Check thickness and segregation separately. Where needed, increase head in a test column and monitor discharged sediment and pressure difference to distinguish material compatibility from installation quality. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將濾料分位粒徑改成三毫米重算比值，畫出可能離析的兩個區域。說明還需要哪些透水與保土試驗，才能在指定基土下作選材判斷。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change the filter percentile size to three millimetres and recompute the ratio. Sketch two possible segregation zones and identify permeability and retention tests needed to choose material for the specified base soil.","failure":"注意干擾：合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。另量施工厚度並檢查離析，必要時在試驗柱施加逐級水頭，觀察出水含砂及壓差，將材料相容與施工品質分開驗證。","textEn":"Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units. Check thickness and segregation separately. Where needed, increase head in a test column and monitor discharged sediment and pressure difference to distinguish material compatibility from installation quality.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將濾料分位粒徑改成三毫米重算比值，畫出可能離析的兩個區域。說明還需要哪些透水與保土試驗，才能在指定基土下作選材判斷。","textEn":"Change the filter percentile size to three millimetres and recompute the ratio. Sketch two possible segregation zones and identify permeability and retention tests needed to choose material for the specified base soil.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「濾層粒徑的相容比較」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Filter grading compatibility\"?","options":["分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠"],"optionsEn":["Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough"],"answer":0,"explanation":"分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b277-v15-28","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較：失效診斷","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濾層粒徑的相容比較」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Filter grading compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。若只查出廠報告而不取現場樣品，會錯把材料證書當成完整濾層性能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones. Factory certificates without installed samples can therefore misrepresent the performance of the completed filter layer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查應連結基土和濾料的完整級配曲線，再用代表水力梯度的試驗觀察濁度、流量與壓力是否穩定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare complete grading curves and use tests at representative hydraulic gradients to observe whether turbidity, discharge and pressure stabilize rather than relying only on sieve labels.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。若只查出廠報告而不取現場樣品，會錯把材料證書當成完整濾層性能。","textEn":"A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones. Factory certificates without installed samples can therefore misrepresent the performance of the completed filter layer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「濾層粒徑的相容比較」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Filter grading compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b277-v15-29","title":"河床泥砂收支：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「河床泥砂收支」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bed sediment continuity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固床工限制高程後仍需允許泥砂進出，否則上游淤積與下游缺砂可能同時發生。固體體積通量的差額除以有效河床面積與固體比例，可估平均床高變化；若輸入數據已含孔隙，再除一次固體比例就會重複放大。這個控制體平均值不表示每個位置均勻升降，實際可能集中於沖坑或沙洲。量測計畫應同時追蹤邊界輸砂和內部地形，才能檢查收支閉合。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「河床泥砂收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Grade control must accommodate sediment continuity or upstream deposition and downstream sediment deficit can coexist. Net solid-volume flux divided by bed area and solid fraction estimates mean bed-level change. If input volumes already include pores, another porosity correction double counts the effect. The control-volume average does not imply uniform change at every point; adjustment may concentrate in holes or bars. Monitor both boundary transport and internal topography to test whether the sediment budget closes. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bed sediment continuity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「河床泥砂收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bed sediment continuity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-29-k1","title":"河床泥砂收支","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity","text":"固床工限制高程後仍需允許泥砂進出，否則上游淤積與下游缺砂可能同時發生。固體體積通量的差額除以有效河床面積與固體比例，可估平均床高變化；若輸入數據已含孔隙，再除一次固體比例就會重複放大。","textEn":"Grade control must accommodate sediment continuity or upstream deposition and downstream sediment deficit can coexist. Net solid-volume flux divided by bed area and solid fraction estimates mean bed-level change.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「河床泥砂收支」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bed sediment continuity\" is correct?","options":["平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","固床工限制高程後仍需允許泥砂進出，否則上游淤積與下游缺砂可能同時發生。"],"optionsEn":["Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","Grade control must accommodate sediment continuity or upstream deposition and downstream sediment deficit can coexist."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固床工限制高程後仍需允許泥砂進出，否則上游淤積與下游缺砂可能同時發生。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Grade control must accommodate sediment continuity or upstream deposition and downstream sediment deficit can coexist. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b277-v15-30","title":"河床泥砂收支：定量估算","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「河床泥砂收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bed sediment continuity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。適用邊界：固體體積通量且無側向輸砂，負值代表控制體平均侵蝕。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m. Applicable boundary: Solid-volume transport without lateral sediment exchange; negative change denotes mean control-volume erosion. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。適用邊界：固體體積通量且無側向輸砂，負值代表控制體平均侵蝕。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m. Applicable boundary: Solid-volume transport without lateral sediment exchange; negative change denotes mean control-volume erosion.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「河床泥砂收支」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bed sediment continuity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b277-v15-31","title":"河床泥砂收支：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「河床泥砂收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bed sediment continuity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。分列岸崩、支流和清淤量，將地形推算的體積差與邊界通量積分核對，並保留採樣誤差範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density. Account separately for bank failure, tributaries and excavation. Compare surveyed volume change with integrated boundary fluxes while retaining sampling uncertainty for both estimates. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持總固體虧損不變，假設侵蝕只集中在四分之一面積，計算該區平均下切。說明控制體平均與局部最大值的差別，並安排能辨認集中侵蝕的測線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep total solid deficit fixed but concentrate erosion over one quarter of the area. Calculate local mean lowering, distinguish it from the whole-reach mean and local maximum, and place transects to detect concentration.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。分列岸崩、支流和清淤量，將地形推算的體積差與邊界通量積分核對，並保留採樣誤差範圍。","textEn":"Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density. Account separately for bank failure, tributaries and excavation. Compare surveyed volume change with integrated boundary fluxes while retaining sampling uncertainty for both estimates.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持總固體虧損不變，假設侵蝕只集中在四分之一面積，計算該區平均下切。說明控制體平均與局部最大值的差別，並安排能辨認集中侵蝕的測線。","textEn":"Keep total solid deficit fixed but concentrate erosion over one quarter of the area. Calculate local mean lowering, distinguish it from the whole-reach mean and local maximum, and place transects to detect concentration.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「河床泥砂收支」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bed sediment continuity\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density.","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b277-v15-32","title":"河床泥砂收支：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「河床泥砂收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bed sediment continuity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。收支不閉合時應逐項查來源，不宜直接調孔隙率湊出答案。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion. When the budget does not close, investigate missing terms rather than adjusting porosity simply to force agreement with surveys. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：量測計畫應同時追蹤邊界輸砂和內部地形，才能檢查收支閉合。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Monitor both boundary transport and internal topography to test whether the sediment budget closes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。收支不閉合時應逐項查來源，不宜直接調孔隙率湊出答案。","textEn":"Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion. When the budget does not close, investigate missing terms rather than adjusting porosity simply to force agreement with surveys.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「河床泥砂收支」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bed sediment continuity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b277-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「塊石浸水重量」與「遷移陡坎的追蹤」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Submerged weight of loose rock\" and \"Tracking migrating bed steps\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-33","title":"塊石浸水重量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「塊石浸水重量」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Submerged weight of loose rock” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"塊石抗移動的一部分來自浸水重量，水下浮力會減少可提供的法向力，但拖曳、升力與支點位置才共同決定滑動或翻滾。球形假設便於建立體積尺度，真實塊石的角狀、扁平與互鎖不能由同一粒徑完全描述。較重也不保證穩定，因為大尺寸可能同時增加迎流面積。分析應先畫自由體圖，再決定需要摩擦、力矩或群體排列試驗，而不是只比較乾重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「塊石浸水重量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Submerged weight contributes to rock resistance, but drag, lift and pivot geometry jointly govern sliding or rolling. A sphere provides a transparent volume scale; angularity, flatness and interlocking of real stones are not captured by one diameter. Greater mass does not automatically mean stability because larger stones also expose more frontal area. Draw the free-body diagram before selecting friction, moment or arrangement tests, and distinguish a weight calculation from a complete stability assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Submerged weight of loose rock” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「塊石浸水重量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Submerged weight of loose rock”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-33-k1","title":"塊石浸水重量","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock","text":"塊石抗移動的一部分來自浸水重量，水下浮力會減少可提供的法向力，但拖曳、升力與支點位置才共同決定滑動或翻滾。球形假設便於建立體積尺度，真實塊石的角狀、扁平與互鎖不能由同一粒徑完全描述。","textEn":"Submerged weight contributes to rock resistance, but drag, lift and pivot geometry jointly govern sliding or rolling. A sphere provides a transparent volume scale; angularity, flatness and interlocking of real stones are not captured by one diameter.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塊石浸水重量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Submerged weight of loose rock\" is correct?","options":["塊石抗移動的一部分來自浸水重量，水下浮力會減少可提供的法向力，但拖曳、升力與支點位置才共同決定滑動或翻滾。","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度"],"optionsEn":["Submerged weight contributes to rock resistance, but drag, lift and pivot geometry jointly govern sliding or rolling.","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"塊石抗移動的一部分來自浸水重量，水下浮力會減少可提供的法向力，但拖曳、升力與支點位置才共同決定滑動或翻滾。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Submerged weight contributes to rock resistance, but drag, lift and pivot geometry jointly govern sliding or rolling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b277-v15-34","title":"塊石浸水重量：定量估算","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塊石浸水重量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Submerged weight of loose rock” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。適用邊界：完全浸沒理想球體的重量尺度，未計升力、拖曳或互鎖。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N. Applicable boundary: Submerged ideal-sphere weight scale, excluding lift, drag and interlocking. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。適用邊界：完全浸沒理想球體的重量尺度，未計升力、拖曳或互鎖。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N. Applicable boundary: Submerged ideal-sphere weight scale, excluding lift, drag and interlocking.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塊石浸水重量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Submerged weight of loose rock\", which statement holds?","options":["不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。","共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠"],"optionsEn":["Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3.","A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b277-v15-35","title":"塊石浸水重量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塊石浸水重量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Submerged weight of loose rock” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。於代表鋪排方式下觀察最先移動的石塊與支點，並記錄它是滑動或翻滾，避免只以平均重量判定整層材料表現。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation. Test representative arrangements and identify the first moving stone and pivot. Record sliding versus rolling rather than judging the entire layer from average weight alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將等效直徑增加百分之十，計算浸水重量增加比例，再比較迎流面積的增加比例。畫出一塊石的可能支點，指出仍缺哪些荷載才能判斷翻滾。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase equivalent diameter by ten percent and compare the weight increase with frontal-area growth. Draw a possible pivot for one stone and identify the additional loads required before assessing rolling resistance.","failure":"注意干擾：扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。於代表鋪排方式下觀察最先移動的石塊與支點，並記錄它是滑動或翻滾，避免只以平均重量判定整層材料表現。","textEn":"Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation. Test representative arrangements and identify the first moving stone and pivot. Record sliding versus rolling rather than judging the entire layer from average weight alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將等效直徑增加百分之十，計算浸水重量增加比例，再比較迎流面積的增加比例。畫出一塊石的可能支點，指出仍缺哪些荷載才能判斷翻滾。","textEn":"Increase equivalent diameter by ten percent and compare the weight increase with frontal-area growth. Draw a possible pivot for one stone and identify the additional loads required before assessing rolling resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塊石浸水重量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Submerged weight of loose rock\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b277-v15-36","title":"塊石浸水重量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塊石浸水重量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Submerged weight of loose rock” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。若局部石塊先失去互鎖，後續移動會增加，應檢查鋪排而不只換更重材料。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass. Local loss of interlock can trigger further movement, calling for arrangement checks before simply specifying heavier material. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分析應先畫自由體圖，再決定需要摩擦、力矩或群體排列試驗，而不是只比較乾重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Draw the free-body diagram before selecting friction, moment or arrangement tests, and distinguish a weight calculation from a complete stability assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。若局部石塊先失去互鎖，後續移動會增加，應檢查鋪排而不只換更重材料。","textEn":"A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass. Local loss of interlock can trigger further movement, calling for arrangement checks before simply specifying heavier material.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塊石浸水重量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Submerged weight of loose rock\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度"],"optionsEn":["A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b277-v15-37","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「遷移陡坎的追蹤」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tracking migrating bed steps” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河床陡坎可能沿河道向上游遷移，把下游擾動傳到支流或基礎附近。重複測量其位置可求期間平均移動速率，但侵蝕通常集中在少數洪水，不能把多年平均當成每日固定速度。里程方向必須先定義，否則正負號容易被解讀相反。調查也需區分同一陡坎移動與新陡坎形成，並配合床質、落差和事件流量辨認過程，避免只把兩個影像點連線外推。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「遷移陡坎的追蹤」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A bed step can migrate upstream and transmit downstream disturbance toward tributaries or foundations. Repeated positions give an interval-average migration rate, but erosion often occurs during a few floods rather than at a constant daily speed. Define chainage direction before interpreting signs. Distinguish movement of the same step from creation of a new one, and combine positions with bed material, drop height and event flows instead of extrapolating a line between two images. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tracking migrating bed steps” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「遷移陡坎的追蹤」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tracking migrating bed steps”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-37-k1","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps","text":"河床陡坎可能沿河道向上游遷移，把下游擾動傳到支流或基礎附近。重複測量其位置可求期間平均移動速率，但侵蝕通常集中在少數洪水，不能把多年平均當成每日固定速度。","textEn":"A bed step can migrate upstream and transmit downstream disturbance toward tributaries or foundations. Repeated positions give an interval-average migration rate, but erosion often occurs during a few floods rather than at a constant daily speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「遷移陡坎的追蹤」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tracking migrating bed steps\" is correct?","options":["兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度","河床陡坎可能沿河道向上游遷移，把下游擾動傳到支流或基礎附近。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距"],"optionsEn":["The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration","A bed step can migrate upstream and transmit downstream disturbance toward tributaries or foundations.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"河床陡坎可能沿河道向上游遷移，把下游擾動傳到支流或基礎附近。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A bed step can migrate upstream and transmit downstream disturbance toward tributaries or foundations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b277-v15-38","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤：定量估算","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「遷移陡坎的追蹤」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tracking migrating bed steps” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。適用邊界：相同陡坎之期間平均向上游速率，不是未來事件預測。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream. Applicable boundary: Interval-average upstream rate for the same bed step, not a forecast of future events. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。適用邊界：相同陡坎之期間平均向上游速率，不是未來事件預測。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream. Applicable boundary: Interval-average upstream rate for the same bed step, not a forecast of future events.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「遷移陡坎的追蹤」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tracking migrating bed steps\", which statement holds?","options":["臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。"],"optionsEn":["Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b277-v15-39","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「遷移陡坎的追蹤」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tracking migrating bed steps” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。將每次洪水後的位置加到時間軸，保留位置誤差；如果只有兩期資料，應明確報告平均值而不畫成已知連續速度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature. Add post-flood positions to a timeline with uncertainty. With only two surveys, report an interval mean rather than a known continuous velocity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：若兩次位置各有兩公尺可能誤差，估算速率的最保守範圍。提出洪水後加測的時間安排，說明新增資料如何區分事件跳躍與穩定緩慢遷移。","observationEn":"Site practice: Allow two metres of possible error at each position and estimate conservative rate bounds. Plan post-flood surveys and explain how additional observations would distinguish event-driven jumps from steady slow migration.","failure":"注意干擾：不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。將每次洪水後的位置加到時間軸，保留位置誤差；如果只有兩期資料，應明確報告平均值而不畫成已知連續速度。","textEn":"Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature. Add post-flood positions to a timeline with uncertainty. With only two surveys, report an interval mean rather than a known continuous velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"若兩次位置各有兩公尺可能誤差，估算速率的最保守範圍。提出洪水後加測的時間安排，說明新增資料如何區分事件跳躍與穩定緩慢遷移。","textEn":"Allow two metres of possible error at each position and estimate conservative rate bounds. Plan post-flood surveys and explain how additional observations would distinguish event-driven jumps from steady slow migration.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「遷移陡坎的追蹤」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tracking migrating bed steps\"?","options":["以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全"],"optionsEn":["Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b277-v15-40","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「遷移陡坎的追蹤」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tracking migrating bed steps” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。先核對特徵身分與基準，再討論是否需要額外防護，避免依假速率加碼工程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement. Verify feature identity and survey datum before using the apparent rate to justify additional protective works upstream. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：調查也需區分同一陡坎移動與新陡坎形成，並配合床質、落差和事件流量辨認過程，避免只把兩個影像點連線外推。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Distinguish movement of the same step from creation of a new one, and combine positions with bed material, drop height and event flows instead of extrapolating a line between two images.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。先核對特徵身分與基準，再討論是否需要額外防護，避免依假速率加碼工程。","textEn":"Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement. Verify feature identity and survey datum before using the apparent rate to justify additional protective works upstream.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「遷移陡坎的追蹤」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tracking migrating bed steps\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
